# forge/sheen/iridescent: the iridescent tell (28.7): the row cuts' alternate courses recoloured to Metal 2 keeping the
# step (the hue-turned ramp), keyed by the cut, so the scales and plates alternate two hues course by course; on any
# other cut the rest view turns every third row.
# FORGE-MARKS, forge i2 (tools: emb_P2c/forge/areas/FORGE-MARKS/tools2/mk2.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# SHEEN TELL (STYLE_P2 28.7; asks FORGE-DOLL to lay it as a cut tile after the cut when the body's sheen is this one):
# the iridescent rows recolour alternate courses of the row cuts to Metal 2 keeping the step (P2C_CONTRACTS 3c: an
# iridescent alloy's Metal 2 is its hue-turned ramp, so the courses alternate two hues), keyed by the cut.
use person
role overlay sheen.iridescent
tags tile overlay on-slot:metal
legend + ink 3
legend ^ ink 4
legend : ink 1
legend = ink 0
legend O metal2 2
legend n accent 1
legend o accent 2
legend p accent 3

view D key round origin 0 0
|OOOO
|OOOO
|OOOO
|....
|....
|....

view D key pointed origin 0 0
|OOOO
|OOOO
|OOOO
|....
|....
|....

view D key square origin 0 0
|OOOO
|OOOO
|OOOO
|....
|....
|....

view D key laced origin 0 0
|...
|...
|...
|...
|OOO
|OOO
|OOO
|OOO

view D key staggered origin 0 0
|OOOOOO
|OOOOOO
|OOOOOO
|......
|......
|......

view D key rest origin 0 0
|O
|.
|.
